 Since we want to integrate B's idea explicitly, let's use the prefix-sum horizontal max with SIMD reduction. That will also make the code more clearly using B's transformation.\n\nSo modify:\n\n- Add `std::vector<long long> pref(n+1);` outside loops.\n- In each step (including initial), after colSum is ready:\n  - compute pref[0]=0; for i=0..n-1: pref[i+1] = pref[i]+cs[i];\n  - then `#pragma omp simd reduction(max:mx)` loop over j from 0 to n-s: window = pref[j+s]-pref[j]; if > mx update.\n\nThis replaces the sliding horizontal max. It's O(n) per step but vectorizable in second part.\n\nWe can also do this for initial top row.\n\nLet's rewrite accordingly.\n\nAlso we might want to use `__restrict` on pointers.\n\nNow code:\n\n```cpp\n#include <cstdio>\n#include <vector>\n#include <cstdint>\n\nclass FastScanner {\n    static constexpr int BUFSIZE = 1 << 20;\n    char buf[BUFSIZE];\n    char* cur;\n    char* end;\n    bool refill() {\n        size_t r = fread(buf, 1, BUFSIZE, stdin);\n        cur = buf;\n        end = buf + r;\n        return r > 0;\n    }\npublic:\n    FastScanner() : cur(buf), end(buf) {}\n    inline int nextInt() {\n        while (true) {\n            if (cur == end && !refill()) return 0;\n            char c = *cur++;\n            if (c <= ' ') continue;\n            int sign = 1;\n            if (c == '-') {\n                sign = -1;\n                if (cur == end && !refill()) return 0;\n                c = *cur++;\n            }\n            int x = c - '0';\n            while (true) {\n                if (cur == end && !refill()) break;\n                char d = *cur++;\n                if (d < '0' || d > '9') break;\n                x = x * 10 + (d - '0');\n            }\n            return sign * x;\n        }\n    }\n};\n\nint main() {\n    FastScanner fs;\n    int n = fs.nextInt();\n    int s = fs.nextInt();\n\n    std::vector<long long> colSum(n, 0);\n    std::vector<int> ring((size_t)s * n);\n    std::vector<int> newRow(n);\n    std::vector<long long> pref(n + 1);\n\n    // Read first S rows and initialize column sums.\n    for (int i = 0; i < s; ++i) {\n        int* rowPtr = &ring[(size_t)i * n];\n        int j = 0;\n        for (; j + 3 < n; j += 4) {\n            newRow[j]   = fs.nextInt();\n            newRow[j+1] = fs.nextInt();\n            newRow[j+2] = fs.nextInt();\n            newRow[j+3] = fs.nextInt();\n        }\n        for (; j < n; ++j) newRow[j] = fs.nextInt();\n\n        #pragma omp simd\n        for (int k = 0; k < n; ++k) {\n            rowPtr[k] = newRow[k];\n            colSum[k] += static_cast<long long>(newRow[k]);\n        }\n    }\n\n    // Helper lambda to compute max SxS window from current column sums.\n    auto updateMax = [&](long long& mx) {\n        pref[0] = 0;\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) pref[i+1] = pref[i] + colSum[i];\n        #pragma omp simd reduction(max:mx)\n        for (int j = 0; j <= n - s; ++j) {\n            long long w = pref[j+s] - pref[j];\n            if (w > mx) mx = w;\n        }\n    };\n\n    long long mx = LLONG_MIN;\n    updateMax(mx);\n\n    // Slide the S-row window downward.\n    int nextSlot = 0;\n    const int limit = n - s;\n    for (int step = 1; step <= limit; ++step) {\n        int* rowPtr = &ring[(size_t)nextSlot * n];\n        long long* cs = colSum.data();\n\n        // Read the entire new row into temporary buffer.\n        int j = 0;\n        for (; j + 3 < n; j += 4) {\n            newRow[j]   = fs.nextInt();\n            newRow[j+1] = fs.nextInt();\n            newRow[j+2] = fs.nextInt();\n            newRow[j+3] = fs.nextInt();\n        }\n        for (; j < n; ++j) newRow[j] = fs.nextInt();\n\n        // Update column sums and ring slot with SIMD vectorization.\n        #pragma omp simd\n        for (int k = 0; k < n; ++k) {\n            int v = newRow[k];\n            long long delta = static_cast<long long>(v) - rowPtr[k];\n            rowPtr[k] = v;\n            cs[k] += delta;\n        }\n\n        updateMax(mx);\n\n        ++nextSlot;\n        if (nextSlot == s) nextSlot = 0;\n    }\n\n    std::printf(\"%lld\\n\", static_cast<long long>(mx));\n    return 0;\n}\n```\n\nWe need to include <climits> for LLONG_MIN. Add that.\n\nAlso note: `updateMax` lambda captures colSum by reference; fine.\n\nPotential issue: The prefix computation loop is sequential and might be a bottleneck, but it's simple adds. Could we vectorize it? Not easily due to dependency. But maybe compiler can use SIMD with `#pragma omp simd` on prefix? No, because each element depends on previous. However there are techniques like parallel prefix (scan) but overkill.\n\nAlternatively, keep sliding loop and just add `#pragma omp simd reduction(max:mx)` to a version that computes all windows independently using colSum directly without pref? That would be O(n^2) if done naively. So prefix is needed for vectorization.\n\nGiven B used this approach and got decent time, let's go with it.\n\nWe should also consider using `#pragma omp simd` on the update loop (already there). And maybe on initial colSum accumulation? Not necessary.\n\nNow check correctness: For each step, we compute max over all horizontal windows for current column sums. That gives correct global max because vertical sliding covers all top rows. Yes.\n\nWe must ensure `mx` initialized to LLONG_MIN; but problem guarantees result fits int, so fine.\n\nLet's also add `#include <climits>`.\n\nNow sources_kept: all three ids.\n\nTransformations list:\n- \"Adopted direct-buffer FastScanner with pointer cursors and refill (from A)\"\n- \"Unrolled row reading by 4 to reduce loop overhead (from A)\"\n- \"Retained ring-buffer streaming column-sum approach (A/C)\"\n- \"Used prefix sums and explicit #pragma omp simd reduction(max) for horizontal maximum computation (B)\"\n- \"Kept SIMD vectorized vertical column-sum updates (C)\"\n\nWe'll output JSON.\n\nLet's ensure the code compiles with -O3 and OpenMP. The target is ARM64, g++ likely supports OpenMP 4.5+.